  "changes": [
    "Ported from TypeScript to plain ES modules: no build step, no dependency outside node: builtins.",
    "performance.now() replaced with Date.now() where the port runs inside the gateway sandbox.",
    "zod validation hand-written; filter matching and the severity vocabulary kept as-is.",
    "Progress and trace logging removed; the engines report through ctx.state instead.",
    "Hashes identify the ported copies in this package, not the upstream originals.",
    "License kept as MIT, carrying both the OmniRoute copyright line and this plugin's.",
    "Same turn semantics as history-trim (#423): the turn being sent (everything after the last assistant message, or the whole body when there is none) is left exactly as it arrived. The 21 cases in test/fixtures/approved-lite-cases.json are copied from that package and pass unmodified.",
    "preserve.lastTurns defaults to 0 and the lite engine's preserveCurrentTurn defaults to true: no sliding window rewrites a prefix that was already sent. preserveCurrentTurn: false exists for callers who prefer strict prefix stability over leaving the current turn alone; README says which is which."
  ]
